From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Trinity AI Agent <267220563+trinity-ai-agent@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 18:13:49 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 08/11] TCSocket: optional v2 framing with a CRC and resync

With raw framing the link is a plain run of 376-byte packets. One
lost, extra or changed byte puts every later packet out of step, and
only a new connection fixes it.

Add an opt-in v2 framing (tcd.ini: Framing = v2; the default stays
raw, so an unchanged reflector keeps working). After the one
module-letter byte, each packet, pings too, is sent as:

  'TCD2' | version u8 (1) | flags u8 (0) | length u16 LE |
  payload (TCPacketCodec encoding) | CRC-32/IEEE u32 LE over
  version..payload

The reader (CV2Reader in TCFraming.{h,cpp}) checks magic, version,
length bounds (376..1024, bytes after 376 are ignored so later versions
can add fields) and CRC. A bad frame is counted, logged once per
burst, and skipped: the reader scans forward to the next magic and
goes on. It closes the link only after 8 bad frames in a row or 64 KiB
of bytes outside a frame. A good frame that names another module counts
as a bad frame.

Only the tcd (client) side implements v2. CTCServer refuses to open in
v2 mode.
